@startuml
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
scale max 800 width
skinparam padding 2
skinparam ParticipantPadding 20
skinparam maxMessageSize 150

title Module 3 — Content Studio: End-to-End Pipeline (3.1 → 3.2 → 3.3)

actor Operator as O
participant "ContentStudio\nView" as UI
participant "Content\nController" as CC
participant "ContentGeneration\n/ApprovalService" as CS
participant "CreativeDirection\nController/Service" as CD
participant "Compliance\nController" as CC3
participant "AIInferenceGateway\nService" as GW
participant "FastAPI\n(fastapi-sbert)" as FP
database "PostgreSQL" as DB

== Transaction 3.1 — Market-Localized Promotional Content Generation ==

O -> UI: Open Content Studio (market selected)
UI -> CC: POST /api/v1/content/generate ?profileId
CC -> CS: generate(req, profileId)
CS -> CS: load BusinessProfile + Module 2 forecast context
CS -> GW: generateCaption(payload)
GW -> FP: POST /internal/generation/caption

note right of FP
  LangGraph 2-node agent:
  analyze_services -> generate_platform_captions
  cultural_research + get_platform_guides
  3 archetypes × 3 platforms (+ hardcoded Naver)
end note

FP --> GW: {market, framework, captions, source}
GW --> CS: raw map
CS -> DB: INSERT 4 rows (approval_status = false)\n+ ContentGenerationLog
CS --> CC: ContentResponseDto
CC --> UI: captions matrix
UI -> UI: Render AIContentMatrixPanel

O -> UI: Approve one caption per platform
UI ->> CC: POST /api/v1/content/approve {market} ?profileId
CC -> CS: approveForMarket(profileId, market)
CS -> DB: UPDATE approval_status = true, approved_at = now()
CS --> CC: {approvedIds, market, count}
CC --> UI: approval confirmed

note over CC,DB: approval_status = true is the dependency gate for 3.2

== Transaction 3.2 — Creative Direction and Visual Recommendation Generation ==

O -> UI: Generate creative direction
UI -> CD: POST /api/v1/creative-direction/generate/{profileId} ?market
CD -> CS: hasApprovedContent(profileId, market)

alt no approved 3.1 content (A3)
  CS --> CD: false
  CD --> UI: HTTP 400 {error: "missing_dependency"}
else approved content exists
  CS --> CD: true + getApprovedCaptions()
  CD -> CD: load BusinessProfile + forecast context
  CD -> GW: generateCreative(payload)
  GW -> FP: POST /internal/creative/generate
  note right of FP
    gemini_client.generate_creative_direction()
    visualGuide / shots / moodboard /
    platformRecommendations  (source: groq|fallback)
    Curated per-market fallback on Groq error
  end note
  FP --> GW: CreativeDirectionResponse
  GW --> CD: raw map
  CD -> DB: INSERT tbl_creative_direction_output\n(approval_status = false) + CreativeDirectionLog
  CD --> UI: CreativeDirectionDto {visualGuide, shots, moodboard}
  UI -> UI: Render VisualDirectionBoard
end

O -> UI: Approve creative direction
UI -> CD: POST /api/v1/creative-direction/approve/{profileId} ?market
CD -> DB: UPDATE approval_status = true, approved_at = now()
CD --> UI: {approvedId, market}

== Transaction 3.3 — OMCS Compliance Audit (Stateless) ==

O -> UI: Upload media image + stage caption\n(SmartOptimizationBoard toggle → MediaCaptionManager)
O -> UI: Run audit
UI -> CC3: POST /api/v1/compliance/omcs-analyze\n{caption, imageUrl, businessProfile, recommendations}

note right of CC3
  Validates: caption + imageUrl required.
  Builds payload; delegates to FastAPI.
  No rows are persisted.
end note

CC3 -> GW: analyzeOmcsAgent(payload)
GW -> FP: POST /internal/omcs/analyze

note right of FP
  LangGraph omcs_agent (stateless):
  CAS  = profile semantic alignment   (weight 0.35)
  VAS  = recommendations×picture rubric (weight 0.45)
  HCS  = pubmat caption/image consistency (weight 0.20)
  OMCS = (0.35×CAS) + (0.45×VAS) + (0.20×HCS)
  Pass/Fail threshold: 70
  Returns rubric breakdown + feedback diagnostic on Fail
end note

FP --> GW: {profileSemanticScore, rubricEvaluationData,\nrecommendationsPictureScore, consistencyExplanation,\npubmatConsistencyScore, omcsScore, status, feedback}
GW --> CC3: raw map
CC3 --> UI: OmcsAuditResultDto
UI -> UI: Render SmartOptimizationBoard\n(ComplianceGauge + rubric table + feedback)

@enduml
